How to build it, step by step

1 Pick a dataset with at least several thousand rows and dates in it. Read its description fully.
2 Write five business questions before you touch the data. The questions guide the whole project.
3 Clean the data in notebook 01 and save the cleaned file. Explain each decision in markdown cells.
4 Answer your questions in notebook 02, with one chart per question and a written conclusion under
each chart.
5 Load the cleaned data into PostgreSQL and rewrite at least five of your answers as SQL queries.
Save them in queries.sql.
6 Build the Streamlit app with KPI cards, filters and the main charts.
7 Write the insights and recommendations section in the README in simple business language.

Deployment

Streamlit Community Cloud lets you deploy directly from your GitHub repo. Keep the dataset small
enough for the free tier, or use a sample.

Questions this project prepares you for
• Walk me through how you cleaned this data. Why did you handle missing values that way?
• What was your most surprising finding?
• If the business had money for only one action, what would you recommend and why?
• Write the SQL for the top three products in each region (window functions).
